{"content":"q28.\n\n**Runners the server actually starts** (all wiring in `server/server.go:153-174`, `startBackgroundRunners`):\n\n- **`s3presign.Runner`** — started twice-over: one synchronous `RunOnce(ctx)` at startup (`server/server.go:163`), then a goroutine running `Run(s3Context)` which is driven by a **fixed `time.Ticker` at 12 h** (`runnerInterval = time.Hour * 12`, `server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:27-41`). Per-cycle work is self-throttled: an attachment is re-presigned only if its `LastPresignedTime` is older than 4 days (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:85-91`). Cancelled via a stored `context.CancelFunc` on shutdown (`server/server.go:156-159`, `176-182`).\n- **`store/cache` cleanup loop (×3)** — not registered as a \"background runner,\" but three long-lived goroutines are started implicitly when the store is constructed: `cache.New` spawns `go c.cleanupLoop()` (`store/cache/cache.go:83`) for `instanceSettingCache`, `userCache`, `userSettingCache` (`store/store.go:51-53`). Driven by a **`time.Ticker` on `CleanupInterval = 5 min`** (`store/cache/cache.go:201`, config at `store/store.go:42`). Stopped via `Close()`/`stopChan` (`store/cache/cache.go:187-197`).\n\nThat is the whole set. Everything else async in the server is **request-scoped, not scheduled**:\n- SSE heartbeat ticker lives inside the per-connection handler (`server/router/api/v1/sse_handler.go:64`), one per client, ends with the request.\n- PAT last-used write is a fire-and-forget goroutine per authentication (`server/auth/authenticator.go:180`).\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:**\n\n- **`internal/scheduler` — a complete cron scheduler that the server never uses.** It has cron-expression parsing (`internal/scheduler/parser.go`), job registration and a `Start`/`Stop` lifecycle (`internal/scheduler/scheduler.go:70`, `:91`, `:169`), timezone support, and `Recovery`/`Logging`/`Timeout` middleware (`internal/scheduler/middleware.go`), plus a README and `doc.go`. The only importers of `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/scheduler` are its own tests — `internal/scheduler/example_test.go:10` and `internal/scheduler/integration_test.go:13`. The code graph returns a certified zero for callers of `Scheduler.Start` outside the package. `server/server.go` does not import it; the one real periodic job (s3presign) hand-rolls a ticker instead.\n- **`server/runner/memopayload.Runner` — a runner type that is never started.** `NewRunner` / `RunOnce` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:19`, `:27`) have no callers; the only use of that package is the pure helper `RebuildMemoPayload`, called inline on the request path in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108` and `:447`. So the backfill-all-memos path exists but nothing triggers it.","iteration":15,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
